Let me say it again (since it seems that my comments usually don't get any
form of reply).

The key point is that we have tons of people DISCUSSING ABOUT the language
and very few people actually USING it.

What is worse is that the migration to MediaWiki broke most of the links to
existing material (e.g. this is one of my translations, try to link on the
PDF file! https://mw.lojban.org/papri/File:lenumakfaprami.pdf ), probably
discouraging people to contribute with more material.

The only way, to me, to make the language evolve is to actually doing
something with it. The key points, imho, that make Lojban and should never
be abandonded are:

 - Statement as relation (as opposed to Subject/Verb/objects)
 - Formal grammar to resolve any parsing ambiguity (I really welcomed
moving to PEG).

mu'e mi'e la .remod.



